# Mail Reader OAuth configuration — YOU DON'T NEED TO EDIT THIS FILE.
#
# On first use the app itself opens the "Set up OAuth" screen with a tutorial:
# you paste the codes there and it creates/updates this machine's .env on its own.
#
# This file only exists as a reference of the variables used (and for whoever
# prefers to fill them in by hand: copy it to .env and edit it).
#
# The .env is LOCAL and is in .gitignore — never commit your credentials.
# On another computer: copy your .env there, or paste the codes into the app again.

# Google Cloud → Credentials → OAuth client ID → type "Desktop app"
# The ID ends in .apps.googleusercontent.com; the "secret" starts with GOCSPX-
MAIL_READER_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
MAIL_READER_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Azure → App registrations → Application (client) ID
MAIL_READER_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
